{
  "methodology": "Storage-format microbenchmark: captured real two-step aggregate/finish engine checkpoints, repeated with distinct run ids through native SDK TOON serialization and sealed history diffs. Corpus receipt counts and embedded prompts advance with accumulated roots, including exact prompt-byte accounting. Both arms retain identical checkpoint transitions in history and materialize each final item once; intermediate item flushes and write throughput are excluded. Each source uses its existing eval-design revision in independent plain-directory trackers. No inference, full-engine throughput, provider quality, cold-cache latency or power-loss durability claim. Logical/allocated file bytes include the entire tracker. Timed reads use a separate process per milestone with a 4096 MiB old-space limit and 300000 ms timeout; failures retain null latency and explicit exit/signal/timing evidence. Complete reads are SDK-certified full-item reads; at 10/100 runs, median of three warm samples after one warm-up; at 500 runs, one fresh-process read to keep the same bounded read attempt feasible for both formats.",
